WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
The invoice bills 108 THB per unit. The purchase order says 100 THB. Local AI is selected.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
The model retrieves invoice context, matching results, policy and graph evidence. Actual run time was 53.82 seconds.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Qwen identifies the price mismatch and the need for human review. Its proposed action is hold for review.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:31.000
The reviewer uses the prepared fictional evidence to set the unit price to 100 THB and records the reason.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:39.000
The correction is saved, but approval remains locked until the deterministic checks run against the new values.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Matching checks pass. The reviewer adds a decision note before recording approval. The AI does not approve.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:54.000
The invoice, order and delivery now agree. This is a local synthetic decision, with no payment or SAP posting.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:02.000
The history records the investigation, price correction, successful recheck and human approval.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:10.000
The app identifies the old recommendation as out of date after a correction. Fresh matching checks govern approval.
